---
/**
 * Privacy policy for the Embeddy Android app and the embeddy.link browser
 * tools. Linked from the Play Store listing, the app's About sheet and the
 * site footer. Every statement here must match the code: if a network call
 * is added to the app or the site, update the relevant section.
 */
import ToolLayout from "../layouts/ToolLayout.astro";

const updated = "2026-10-31";
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What Embeddy does with your files and data: no accounts, no analytics, no ads. Processing happens on your device unless you choose to upload or inspect a URL."
>
  <article class="prose-embeddy mx-auto max-w-2xl space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/75">
    <header>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-1 text-white/50">Last updated {updated}. Applies to the Embeddy Android app and the tools at embeddy.link.</p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>Summary</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No accounts, no advertising, no analytics, no crash-reporting SDKs, no tracking.</li>
        <li>Converting, trimming, joining, compressing and reading metadata from a file happens entirely on your device.</li>
        <li>Data leaves your device only when you explicitly use <strong>Upload</strong> or <strong>Inspect a URL</strong>, as described below.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Android app</h2>
      <h3>Files you open</h3>
      <p>
        The app reads only the files you pick with the system file picker or share to it. It does not request
        access to your photo or video library. Intermediate and output files are written to the app's private
        cache and are deleted automatically within 24 hours; files you save go to your Downloads folder.
      </p>
      <h3>Settings</h3>
      <p>
        Your encoder and compression preferences are stored on the device. If Android backup is enabled on your
        device, these preferences may be included in your Google account backup; cached media is excluded.
      </p>
      <h3>Upload</h3>
      <p>
        When you tap Upload, the file you chose is sent directly from your device to the host you selected —
        <a href="https://0x0.st" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">0x0.st</a> or
        <a href="https://catbox.moe" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">catbox.moe</a>. Uploads are
        <strong>public</strong>: anyone with the link can download the file. The host receives your IP address and
        the file, and its own terms and retention rules apply. Embeddy's operator does not receive a copy. For JPEG,
        PNG and WebP files the app can strip EXIF metadata (including GPS location) before upload; it warns you when a
        format cannot be stripped.
      </p>
      <h3>Inspect a URL</h3>
      <p>
        When you inspect a web address, the app requests that page directly from your device to read its
        Open Graph and Twitter tags. The website you inspect sees an ordinary request from your IP address.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Browser tools (embeddy.link)</h2>
      <p>
        The site is static and served by GitHub Pages, which, like any web host, processes your IP address to
        deliver the pages. Fonts and code are self-hosted; no third-party scripts, cookies or analytics are
        loaded. A service worker caches the site for offline use, in your browser only.
      </p>
      <p>
        Convert, trim/join and Squoosh run locally in your browser; files are never uploaded. Inspecting a local
        file also runs locally.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Inspect a URL</strong> and <strong>Upload</strong> cannot be done directly from a browser because of
        cross-origin restrictions, so they go through Embeddy's relay at <code>api.embeddy.link</code>, a Cloudflare
        Worker. The relay fetches the page you asked about, or forwards your file to the host you chose, and returns
        the result. It does not store files or page contents. Metadata stripping for uploads (JPEG, PNG, WebP)
        happens in your browser before the file is sent, and the upload is cancelled if stripping fails. Cloudflare keeps short-lived request logs (time, path,
        status and similar request metadata) for operating and debugging the relay; these are not used for any other
        purpose.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>Embeddy is a general-purpose tool and is not directed at children.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>
        Changes to this policy are published on this page and in the
        <a href="https://github.com/tribixbite/Embeddy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">source repository</a>.
        Questions: open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/tribixbite/Embeddy/issues" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</ToolLayout>

<style>
  /* Minimal prose styling scoped to this article (no typography plugin). */
  .prose-embeddy :global(h2) {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: white;
  }
  .prose-embeddy :global(h3) {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.9);
  }
  .prose-embeddy :global(ul) {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }
  .prose-embeddy :global(li + li) {
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }
  .prose-embeddy :global(a) {
    color: var(--color-brand-300);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .prose-embeddy :global(code) {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }
</style>
